================================================================================
Third-party test fixtures
================================================================================

Some files used only for tests and benchmarks are real HTML pages from the
Wikimedia projects (Wiktionary), retrieved from *.wiktionary.org. They are
included solely to exercise the parser, formatter, and CSS engine against
real-world markup.

These pages are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
License (CC BY-SA); some embedded content may also be available under the GNU
Free Documentation License. See https://www.wiktionary.org and
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ for details.

Affected paths (test/bench data only — not part of the distributed library):
  - crates/htmlarc-dom/src/**/tests/html/*.html
  - crates/htmlarc-dom/src/**/snapshots/*.snap
  - cli/htmlarc/src/testdata/*.html

================================================================================
ZIM support (zim2htmlarc)
================================================================================

The `zim2htmlarc` binary reads the ZIM format via the third-party `zim` crate,
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, pulled in at build time as a Cargo git dependency.
We use a fork (https://github.com/akesson/zim) of the unmaintained upstream
(https://crates.io/crates/zim) that adds support for modern ZIM files. No ZIM
file is bundled in this repository; the optional end-to-end test fetches one on
demand (see cli/zim2htmlarc/fetch-testdata.sh).
